# Math Research v8 continuation prompt

Use this prompt only inside a **current product Goal task**. Normally it resumes the same v8 Goal binding; an explicitly user-created new Goal may use only the special v8 rebind or legacy-successor gates below. The word “heartbeat” in this asset name is historical; this template does not define an external scheduler, dispatcher, timer service, or isolated CLI continuation.

Project directory: `{{PROJECT_DIRECTORY}}`

1. Invoke `$math-research-solve` and run Startup Router v3 as a strict read-only classifier.
2. Call `get_goal` freshly in this current task. Ordinary mutation requires its objective hash to match the effective external host-binding head. A stable task/thread ID is checked only when exposed. `HOST_REBIND` is the sole exception and follows step 6; a new raw hash need not equal the obsolete one.
3. If the Goal is `active` and the single `project.json` head correctly hashes `state/generations/gNNNN/{checkpoint.json,goal-host-v8.json}`, let the model Goal Host continue the unique lifecycle point. Never dispatch the `source_event=null` preparing seed: `ATTEMPT_START` must freeze and activate a new non-null-event solver ticket bound to post-start counters before dispatch. Every `ATTEMPT_END` must publish exact `math-research-attempt-outcome/v8`; `candidate_found` closes the current derived verifier ticket on one exact PASS-bound candidate. Its pre-audit `completion_candidate` permits only terminal `AUDIT_START` or an outcome-preserving `HOST_REBIND`. `goal_host_completion_ready_to_publish` permits only the fresh-gated `COMPLETION_READY` publication; both completion flags true permits only step 9. Do not call an external dispatcher, old Resume command, cycle CLI, or Goal-owning `codex exec` child.
4. Before every attempt, audit, authoritative publication, handoff, pause, closing, rebind, or completion, call `get_goal` again. Admit every new attempt only if the old counters satisfy `attempt_count + 1 <= attempt_budget` and `total_round_count + 2 <= total_round_budget`, preserving a mandatory terminal-audit round even off-interval. Cycle-audit plan/summary/reports bind the same candidate: terminal uses the Attempt outcome candidate, scheduled/early use null. A candidate discovered when an interval/final audit is due runs terminal audit first and clears the gate once. Use collaboration subagents only for frozen hash-bound solver, verifier, or auditor tickets. Children never inspect or mutate Goal control.
5. If Goal is absent, cancelled, paused, blocked, or complete, perform read-only verification/reporting only. A project run whose head is `paused` may next publish only `RESUME` or an exact capsule-preserving `HOST_REBIND`; `CHECKPOINT_COMMIT` and all other events fail closed. Do not dispatch work, backfill state, create/resume/replace a Goal, or claim that this prompt is a live heartbeat.
6. If this is a different task without explicit user revocation of the old binding plus new Goal/rebind authorization, report read-only. For an existing v8 run, user revocation is sufficient—do not query the old task. Require the new Goal freshly active, no unfinished commit, and unchanged Contract semantics/permissions/run identity; the new Host stages one exact-schema `HOST_REBIND` whose `prior_host_binding` equals the old head and whose `retirement` contains `authority=user-explicit-revocation` plus a nonempty reason, along with the new `host_goal`. There is no separate `HOST_RETIRE`. Increment control generation and, after the fresh gate, invoke `scripts/commit_math_research_head_v8.ps1` last.
7. If startup returns `goal_continuity_terminal`, return `stop_no_retry_preserve_run` for the legacy old run. Never Tick/Resume the legacy child, recreate its Goal, rewrite its manifest, repeat migration, or reset counters. Separately, an explicitly user-created new active Goal may create a new v8 `LEGACY_SUCCESSOR` only when the normalized effective predecessor envelope and the new Contract are equivalent in target/domain/quantifiers/dependencies/assumptions/completion, model/reasoning, privacy/external effects, and all agent/runtime/attempt/audit/round/cumulative ceilings, with no permission or resource expansion. Mandatory retirement of the old child-Goal/launcher/dispatcher/lease/control-receipt path and replacement by current-Goal Host + bounded collaboration + head helper is the sole permitted safe contraction, not a mismatch. A same-project `/goal` request to continue until proof/disproof is launch intent; do not request repeated confirmation, hashes, or commands. The model Host must decide same-target natural-language equivalence before calling any script. After a fresh active Goal check, call `scripts/build_math_research_legacy_successor_v8.ps1` through its production observer phase with the project, exact raw Goal objective/raw UTF-8 hash, and optional stable task/thread ID. Require `built=true` and verify its expected-old/new values; it uses Goal text only for external binding, is Goal-agnostic, creates only additive unreferenced staging, and never replaces `project.json`. A same-Goal interrupted build may idempotently reuse verified staging; a different raw Goal hash before activation fails closed and grants no staging authority. Preserve every old byte, inherit all research artifacts/counters/budgets, bind the effective-envelope/control-mapping artifacts, then fresh-check Goal again and activate only through `scripts/commit_math_research_head_v8.ps1`. Authority comes from the current active Goal, not legacy receipts or either helper. This is a new run, not old-Goal recovery; every other difference is read-only pending `RUN_SUCCESSOR`.
8. If startup returns `goal_host_closed_review`, remain read-only. Explicit new Goal/Contract input may authorize planning only; no mutation is allowed until a separately implemented and authorized `RUN_SUCCESSOR` exists. If startup returns `goal_host_state_invalid` or `legacy_execution_unsupported`, stop at `fail_closed_read_only_diagnosis`.
9. Completion flags are valid only as both false or both true. Only an all-PASS/no-new-math terminal cycle audit can return `goal_host_completion_ready_to_publish`; terminal FAIL/INCONCLUSIVE must return to noncompletion and cannot publish `COMPLETION_READY`. Fresh-check and publish only `COMPLETION_READY`, preserving the exact Attempt outcome and terminal summary/history through any permitted rebind. After persisting/activating/reading back both true, project/head state is permanently read-only: never clear them, resume, audit, or publish. Startup then returns `goal_host_completion_pending`; call `get_goal` again immediately before `update_goal(status=complete)`, and call it only if active/matching, with no project write. A complete Goal is closed review; any other non-active Goal remains read-only pending.

When an active Contract has `approval_mode=approve_for_me`, submit only narrow in-envelope `require_escalated` requests to `managed auto-review`; never ask the user to relay a command or hash. A platform denial does not authorize a bypass.

Legacy-only compatibility wording: the historical `scheduler host`, `child`, and `manifest` are separate frozen records. They provide no current Goal continuity or execution authority.
